<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Anastasius I Dicorus</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 430–518</span> · <a href="/centuries/5th-century">5th century</a> · Also known as Anastasius I</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Anastasius I was emperor of the Eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-empire">Roman Empire</a> from 491 to 518. A palace official chosen by the widowed empress <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ariadne">Ariadne</a>, he reformed the coinage and taxation, leaving a large surplus in the treasury, and fought a war with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/persia">Persia</a> from 502 to 506. His sympathy for Miaphysite views provoked revolts, and his treaty of around 502 made the Ghassanids the empire's leading Arab allies.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/anastasius-i-dicorus.jpg" alt="Anastasius I Dicorus" width="320" height="312" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CNG · CC BY-SA 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Anastasius_I._minted_507-518.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>The emperor <b>Anastasius</b> granted him an honorary consulship, and in his last years Clovis eliminated the rulers of the other Frankish groups, such as Sigibert of Cologne, made Paris his chief residence and summoned a church council at Orléans in 511, the year he died.</blockquote><a href="/empire/kingdom-of-the-franks">Kingdom of the Franks · Foundation</a></li><li><blockquote><b>Anastasius I Dicorus</b>, a career civil servant aged 61, became Eastern Roman emperor after being chosen by Ariadne, the widow of his predecessor Zeno.</blockquote><a href="/today-in-history/april-11">11 April in history</a></li><li><blockquote>Entering Roman territory in the late 5th century, they defeated the Salihids and around 502 made a treaty with the emperor <b>Anastasius</b> that made them the empire's chief Arab allies in Syria and Arabia.</blockquote><a href="/state/ghassanids">Ghassanids</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Born in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/durres">Durrës</a>, in what is now <a href="/countries/albania">Albania</a>. Died in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constantinople">Constantinople</a>, in what is now <a href="/countries/turkey">Turkey</a>. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=41.31,19.45&amp;year=487" aria-label="Durrës on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5025 690 900 540" role="img" aria-label="Map: the birthplace of Anastasius I Dicorus"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5475 960h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5475 960h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the birthplace. <a href="/atlas?at=41.31,19.45&amp;year=487">What was here in 487 CE? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
